{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The lexicographically first minimum vertex cover: of the smallest vertex covers, the least"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by vertex index (the rule of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet()"},{"type":"text","text":": of two covers"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of one size, the lesser holds the least vertex of their symmetric difference), in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order; [] for the empty graph. Every vertex with a self-loop is in it; parallel edges count"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"once."}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/lexicographicallyFirstMinimumVertexCover()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering","doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumVertexCover"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"It is the complement of the lexicographically greatest maximum independent set, not of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"least one: the least vertex of a symmetric difference is in one cover exactly when it is in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the other cover’s complement. That set is found as in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", with each choice the other way round: the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"core pass on a bipartite component leaves out each vertex it decides, a complete component","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"keeps its greatest vertex, and any other component deletes a vertex whenever a maximum set","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"without it remains, with the reductions taking a simplicial vertex greater than all its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"neighbours. The cost is that of ","type":"text"},{"code":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": O(m √n) on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"bipartite components, and up to c exponential searches on a component of c vertices the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reductions do not settle. The search does not check for task cancellation.","type":"text"}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/lexicographicallyfirstminimumvertexcover()"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"metadata":{"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Covering\/ExactCovering.swift#L1739","fileName":"ExactCovering.swift"},"extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P8CoveringE40lexicographicallyFirstMinimumVertexCoverSay0G0QzGyF","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"Covering","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"symbolKind":"method","roleHeading":"Instance Method","title":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumVertexCover()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"t